communicating-vessels-aside-pergamon = Water rises to its own level, and the ancient Greeks made use of it. In Pergamon (now in Turkey), in the 2nd century BC, water was brought to the acropolis across a valley: it ran down a pipe and up the other side. The pressure in this inverted siphon matched a column of water about 190 m high.
